<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cāiēta</span></b> , ae (and
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ē</span></b> , ēs),
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καιήτη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The nurse of Æneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
			443</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town and harbor in Latium</i>, now <i>Gaëta</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or.
				2, 6, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Imp. Pomp. 12, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
				900</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 531</span></i>; Serv. ad Verg. l. l.;
				<i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Orig. Rom. 10</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cāiētānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Caieta</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">villa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 1, 4, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
